{"choices":[{"message":{"content":"{\n  \"chapter_proposals\": [\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"Ch3\",\n      \"title\": \"微生物代谢物的中介作用与分子机制\",\n      \"purpose\": \"深入分析关键微生物代谢物（SCFAs、肌苷、胆汁酸、色氨酸代谢物等）在调节 ICI 疗效中的具体分子机制，区分血浆与肿瘤微环境（TME）浓度数据，阐明代谢物作用的分子靶点（如 UBA6、A2AR、HDAC、AhR）及下游信号通路，并评估现有证据中人体 TME 代谢物浓度数据的缺失情况。\",\n      \"scope\": \"涵盖短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）、肌苷（Inosine）、胆汁酸（Bile Acids）、色氨酸代谢物（Tryptophan metabolites）及其他潜在代谢介质（如 TMAO、多胺）。重点分析代谢物对免疫细胞（T 细胞、DC、巨噬细胞）及肿瘤细胞内在属性（免疫原性、MHC 表达）的调节机制。严格区分动物模型机制与人类临床数据，明确标注人体 TME 内代谢物绝对浓度数据的缺失，仅使用血浆数据作为系统性暴露的代理。\",\n      \"source_handles\": [\n        \"P0582\",\n        \"P0092\",\n        \"P0223\",\n        \"P0503\",\n        \"P0515\",\n        \"P0559\",\n        \"P0180\",\n        \"P0424\",\n        \"P0481\",\n        \"P0139\",\n        \"P0305\",\n        \"P0220\",\n        \"P0317\",\n        \"P0413\",\n        \"P0363\",\n        \"P0584\",\n        \"P0124\",\n        \"P0251\",\n        \"P0444\",\n        \"P0510\",\n        \"P0577\",\n        \"P0195\",\n        \"P0553\",\n        \"P0486\",\n        \"P0518\",\n        \"P0372\",\n        \"P0377\",\n        \"P0506\",\n        \"P0544\",\n        \"P0555\",\n        \"P0563\",\n        \"P0476\",\n        \"P0477\",\n        \"P0319\",\n        \"P0333\",\n        \"P0433\",\n        \"P0464\",\n        \"P0521\",\n        \"P0522\",\n        \"P0532\",\n        \"P0540\",\n        \"P0543\",\n        \"P0574\",\n        \"P0586\",\n        \"P0587\",\n        \"P0002\",\n        \"P0004\",\n        \"P0011\",\n        \"P0018\",\n        \"P0021\",\n        \"P0027\",\n        \"P0028\",\n        \"P0032\",\n        \"P0033\",\n        \"P0036\",\n        \"P0042\",\n        \"P0043\",\n        \"P0047\",\n        \"P0056\",\n        \"P0057\",\n        \"P0059\",\n        \"P0064\",\n        \"P0075\",\n        \"P0076\",\n        \"P0080\",\n        \"P0109\",\n        \"P0113\",\n        \"P0116\",\n        \"P0117\",\n        \"P0120\",\n        \"P0123\",\n        \"P0129\",\n        \"P0137\",\n        \"P0140\",\n        \"P0142\",\n        \"P0144\",\n        \"P0145\",\n        \"P0146\",\n        \"P0148\",\n        \"P0150\",\n        \"P0151\",\n        \"P0152\",\n        \"P0155\",\n        \"P0156\",\n        \"P0158\",\n        \"P0162\",\n        \"P0164\",\n        \"P0165\",\n        \"P0173\",\n        \"P0174\",\n        \"P0176\",\n        \"P0177\",\n        \"P0186\",\n        \"P0192\",\n        \"P0196\",\n        \"P0198\",\n        \"P0201\",\n        \"P0204\",\n        \"P0205\",\n        \"P0209\",\n        \"P0228\",\n        \"P0237\",\n        \"P0247\",\n        \"P0257\",\n        \"P0268\",\n        \"P0282\",\n        \"P0283\",\n        \"P0291\",\n        \"P0293\",\n        \"P0294\",\n        \"P0297\",\n        \"P0303\",\n        \"P0308\",\n        \"P0309\",\n        \"P0320\",\n        \"P0325\",\n        \"P0326\",\n        \"P0330\",\n        \"P0332\",\n        \"P0334\",\n        \"P0337\",\n        \"P0342\",\n        \"P0351\",\n        \"P0355\",\n        \"P0356\",\n        \"P0357\",\n        \"P0369\",\n        \"P0382\",\n        \"P0391\",\n        \"P0401\",\n        \"P0415\",\n        \"P0422\",\n        \"P0427\",\n        \"P0432\",\n        \"P0437\",\n        \"P0439\",\n        \"P0446\",\n        \"P0447\",\n        \"P0451\",\n        \"P0452\",\n        \"P0454\",\n        \"P0455\",\n        \"P0462\",\n        \"P0472\",\n        \"P0473\",\n        \"P0479\",\n        \"P0486\",\n        \"P0496\",\n        \"P0499\",\n        \"P0500\",\n        \"P0507\",\n        \"P0510\",\n        \"P0511\",\n        \"P0514\",\n        \"P0516\",\n        \"P0519\",\n        \"P0523\",\n        \"P0550\",\n        \"P0552\",\n        \"P0554\",\n        \"P0557\",\n        \"P0569\",\n        \"P0571\"\n      ],\n      \"excluded_source_handles\": [\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0024\",\n          \"reason\": \"HIV 感染模型与实体瘤 ICI 背景差异过大，仅作为代谢通路类比，不纳入核心机制论证。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0048\",\n          \"reason\": \"慢性疼痛背景，免疫调节机制虽通用但缺乏肿瘤特异性验证，仅作为背景参考。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0519\",\n          \"reason\": \"代谢疾病背景，表观遗传机制虽相关但缺乏 ICI 疗效直接证据，不纳入核心机制论证。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0542\",\n          \"reason\": \"健康人中药干预研究，免疫稳态与肿瘤患者免疫耗竭状态差异大，不纳入核心机制论证。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"substantive_threads\": [\n        {\n          \"thread_title\": \"短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）的情境依赖性免疫调节\",\n          \"thread_purpose\": \"阐述 SCFAs（乙酸、丙酸、丁酸）通过 HDAC 抑制与 GPCR 信号通路调节免疫细胞功能的双重机制，分析其在不同肿瘤类型（NSCLC/CRC vs. 黑色素瘤）及 ICI 类型（PD-1 vs. CTLA-4）中的效应差异。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0092\",\n            \"P0223\",\n            \"P0503\",\n            \"P0515\",\n            \"P0559\",\n            \"P0377\",\n            \"P0544\"\n          ],\n          \"evidence_summary\": \"临床队列显示粪便 SCFA 水平与 PD-1 抑制剂 PFS 正相关（P0092, P0223），但机制上存在双向性：丁酸盐通过 HDAC 抑制增强 CD8+ T 细胞功能（P0515），但在 CTLA-4 抑制背景下可能抑制 DC 分化（P0503, P0559）。需明确 SCFA 浓度阈值及肿瘤微环境缺氧状态对效应方向的影响。\",\n          \"limitations\": \"多数机制证据来自小鼠模型，人体 TME 内 SCFA 绝对浓度及局部梯度数据缺失，血浆/粪便浓度不能完全代表 TME 暴露水平。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"thread_title\": \"肌苷的肿瘤内在免疫原性调节与 UBA6 机制\",\n          \"thread_purpose\": \"解析肌苷通过抑制肿瘤细胞内 UBA6 酶增强抗原呈递及炎症信号的具体分子路径，评估人体血浆肌苷水平与生存期的关联，并明确指出人体 TME 肌苷浓度数据的缺失。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0582\",\n            \"P0124\",\n            \"P0251\",\n            \"P0584\",\n            \"P0479\"\n          ],\n          \"evidence_summary\": \"肌苷直接结合并抑制肿瘤细胞泛素激活酶 UBA6，解除其对炎症信号及 MHC-I 表达的抑制，增强 T 细胞杀伤敏感性（P0582）。CheckMate 025 试验显示高血浆肌苷与 RCC 患者 ICI 治疗后 OS 延长相关（中位 33 vs. 22 个月），但研究明确说明未在肿瘤组织中直接测量肌苷浓度（P0582）。\",\n          \"limitations\": \"人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度（μM 或 ng/mL）数据缺失，仅有人血浆数据作为系统性暴露代理；机制验证主要依赖小鼠模型及体外实验。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"thread_title\": \"胆汁酸与色氨酸代谢物的核受体信号轴\",\n          \"thread_purpose\": \"阐述次级胆汁酸（TDCA, isoalloLCA）及色氨酸代谢物（IPA, Kynurenine）通过核受体（FXR, TGR5, AhR, RORγt）调节 T 细胞分化及巨噬细胞极化的机制。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0180\",\n            \"P0424\",\n            \"P0481\",\n            \"P0139\",\n            \"P0305\",\n            \"P0209\",\n            \"P0510\"\n          ],\n          \"evidence_summary\": \"次级胆汁酸通过 TGR5 增强 CD8+ T 细胞毒性（P0481），或通过抑制 RORγt 调节 Th17/Treg 平衡（P0180）。色氨酸代谢物 IPA 通过 AhR 激活 CD8+ T 细胞（P0209），而犬尿氨酸积累则抑制 T 细胞（P0139）。HCC 队列显示特定胆汁酸与 ICI 疗效相关（P0424）。\",\n          \"limitations\": \"胆汁酸谱受宿主肝脏代谢及饮食影响巨大，微生物贡献比例难以精确量化；AhR 配体效应具有强烈的细胞类型及浓度依赖性。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"thread_title\": \"代谢重编程与免疫细胞功能整合\",\n          \"thread_purpose\": \"综合代谢物如何通过重塑免疫细胞代谢（糖酵解、氧化磷酸化）及表观遗传状态（组蛋白乙酰化、DNA 甲基化）影响 ICI 疗效，区分受体介导与非受体介导机制。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0220\",\n            \"P0317\",\n            \"P0413\",\n            \"P0363\",\n            \"P0587\",\n            \"P0444\",\n            \"P0553\"\n          ],\n          \"evidence_summary\": \"代谢物不仅作为信号分子（受体介导），还作为碳源或表观遗传修饰底物（如丁酸盐抑制 HDAC）直接重编程免疫细胞代谢状态（P0220, P0587）。特定功能通路（如 MEP 通路、核黄素合成）比分类学特征更能预测疗效（P0444）。\",\n          \"limitations\": \"人体免疫细胞在 TME 内的实时代谢状态难以捕捉，多数代谢流数据来自体外或动物模型；因果链条在人类中尚未完全验证。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"thread_title\": \"证据等级与转化缺口：血浆 vs. 组织浓度\",\n          \"thread_purpose\": \"批判性评估现有代谢物数据的证据等级，强调血浆/粪便浓度与 TME 局部浓度的差异，指出人体 TME 代谢物定量数据的缺失是限制机制确证的关键缺口。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0582\",\n            \"P0363\",\n            \"P0584\",\n            \"P0413\",\n            \"P0515\",\n            \"P0559\"\n          ],\n          \"evidence_summary\": \"现有临床数据多基于血浆或粪便代谢组，缺乏肿瘤组织或间质液的配对定量测量（P0582）。机制研究多依赖小鼠模型，人体验证有限。需明确标注 TME 浓度缺口，避免将动物模型浓度外推至人体。\",\n          \"limitations\": \"未被满足的需求仅限于本次材料支持范围（缺乏人体 TME 肌苷/SCFA 浓度数据），不升级为整个领域缺乏相关研究，但需指出这是限制临床转化的关键证据缺口。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"supplement_requests\": [],\n      \"directed_reads\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷（inosine）的生理浓度及其与 ICI 疗效的具体相关性数据是什么？\",\n          \"reason\": \"现有材料（P0582）明确指出由于样本完整性问题，未能在人类肿瘤队列中直接检测肌苷浓度，仅提供了血浆数据。需确认是否有更新研究填补此缺口，若无，则需在综述中明确标注此为未满足的证据需求。\",\n          \"status\": \"confirmed_missing\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"screened_sources\": []\n}","reasoning_content":"The user wants a chapter proposal for Chapter 3 of a review on the gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) in solid tumors.\nThe chapter title is \"微生物代谢物的中介作用与分子机制\" (Mediating Role and Molecular Mechanisms of Microbial Metabolites).\nI need to plan the substantive content for this chapter based on the provided source routing and research question.\nThe plan must be in JSON format, following the specific schema for `chapter_proposals`.\nI need to ensure I don't just copy the input fields but create a substantive proposal for the chapter structure, themes, sources, and limitations.\nKey constraints from the system prompt:\n- Do not write an intro/abstract/conclusion for the whole review (handled elsewhere).\n- Focus on substantive knowledge and analysis.\n- Distinguish between association and causation, mechanism vs. explanation, migration vs. application.\n- Retain source metadata (source_handle).\n- Do not overclaim (e.g., human TME inosine concentration data is missing).\n- Use the provided `source_routing` to select relevant sources for this chapter.\n- Address the specific `key_questions` and `evidence_notes` for Ch3 provided in the input.\n- Ensure the chapter has a clear argumentative thread, not just a list of papers.\n- Handle the `unresolved_limits` regarding inosine TME concentration and Phase III RCTs carefully (do not upgrade to field-level missingness judgments beyond what materials support).\n- Use Chinese for the content.\n\nPlan for Chapter 3:\n1.  **Purpose**: Analyze specific microbial metabolites (SCFAs, Inosine, Bile Acids, Tryptophan) mediating ICI efficacy. Distinguish plasma vs. TME data. Elucidate molecular targets (e.g., UBA6, A2AR, HDAC, AhR).\n2.  **Themes**:\n    *   Short-Chain Fatty Acids (SCFAs): Context-dependent effects (HDAC inhibition vs. GPCR signaling), tumor type specificity (NSCLC/CRC vs. Melanoma/CTLA-4).\n    *   Inosine: Mechanism (UBA6 inhibition in tumor cells), Clinical data (Plasma OS correlation in RCC, lack of TME concentration data).\n    *   Bile Acids: Secondary bile acids (TDCA, isoalloLCA), Receptors (TGR5, FXR, RORγt), Impact on T cells/DCs.\n    *   Tryptophan Metabolites: Kynurenine/AhR axis, IPA, Dual roles (immunosuppression vs. activation).\n    *   Other Metabolites: TMAO, Polyamines, DAT.\n    *   Mechanism Synthesis: Receptor-mediated vs. Epigenetic vs. Metabolic reprogramming.\n    *   Evidence Gaps: Human TME concentrations, Causal validation in humans.\n3.  **Sources**: Select from `source_routing` where `chapter_ids` includes \"Ch3\". Key sources: P0582 (Inosine/UBA6), P0092 (SCFAs/PD-1), P0124 (Inosine/A2A), P0180 (Bile Acids), P0220 (Metabolites review), P0317 (Metabolites/Receptors), P0413 (Metabolites Enemy/Friend), P0503 (SCFAs context), P0515 (Metabolites Clinical Potential), P0559 (Metabolic mediators), P0582 (Inosine mechanism).\n4.  **Limitations**: Explicitly state that TME inosine concentration is missing (only plasma available). Mechanism often from mice. Context dependency (tumor type, ICI type).\n5.  **Structure**:\n    *   3.1 SCFAs: The Double-Edged Sword (HDAC vs GPCR, PD-1 vs CTLA-4).\n    *   3.2 Inosine: Tumor-Intrinsic Immunogenicity (UBA6 mechanism, Plasma OS data).\n    *   3.3 Bile Acids & Tryptophan: Nuclear Receptor Signaling (TGR5, AhR).\n    *   3.4 Mechanism Integration: Metabolic Reprogramming of Immune Cells.\n    *   3.5 Evidence Gaps: Human TME Concentrations & Causal Chains.\n\nI need to make sure I don't include sources that are excluded or not relevant. I will check the `source_routing` for Ch3 assignment.\nMany sources are assigned to Ch3. I will select a representative subset that covers the key metabolites and mechanisms without overcrowding.\nI must ensure the `excluded_source_handles` only contains sources assigned to Ch3 that are genuinely out of scope for *this specific chapter plan* (e.g., if a source is too general or focuses heavily on another chapter's topic like intervention). However, the instruction says \"Do not silently drop a routed source... when an individual source is genuinely out of scope, name it in excluded_source_handles\". Since many sources are broad reviews covering Ch3, I will keep most but might exclude those that are purely about intervention (Ch5) or clinical association without mechanism (Ch1) if they don't add mechanistic value. Actually, the instruction says \"A source may support multiple chapters\". I will retain sources that have specific usable material for Ch3 mechanisms.\nI will focus on the `substantive_threads` to build the argument.\n\nLet's refine the themes based on the `source_routing` specific usable material for Ch3.\n- Inosine/UBA6: P0582 is critical.\n- SCFAs: P0092, P0223, P0503, P0515, P0559.\n- Bile Acids: P0180, P0424, P0481, P0515.\n- Tryptophan/AhR: P0139, P0305, P0515.\n- General Mechanism/Review: P0220, P0317, P0413, P0503, P0559.\n- Limitations/Gap: P0582 (TME concentration missing), P0363 (Context dependency).\n\nI will structure the JSON response accordingly.\nI need to make sure I don't write the \"Introduction\" or \"Conclusion\" of the whole review. This is just Chapter 3.\nI need to check the `shared_level1_outline` to ensure alignment with Ch3's purpose.\nThe `research_question` is about mechanisms mediating the effect.\nThe `unresolved_limits` mention the lack of human TME inosine concentration. I must reflect this in the chapter plan's limitations section.\n\nOne important constraint: \"Do not silently drop a routed source\". I should check if any source assigned to Ch3 is truly not usable for *this specific chapter's argument*. Since Ch3 is about metabolites and mechanisms, sources that are purely about clinical taxonomy (Ch1) or intervention trials (Ch5) without mechanistic metabolite data might be better placed elsewhere, but if they are routed to Ch3, I should try to use them for mechanism if possible. However, if a source is *only* about clinical association without metabolite mechanism, it might be better excluded from Ch3 to keep focus. But the routing already assigned them. I will try to include them where they offer mechanistic insights or metabolite data. If a source is purely Ch1 (taxonomy) but routed to Ch3 for \"metabolic pathways\", I will use the metabolic pathway part.\nActually, the instruction says \"when an individual source is genuinely out of scope, name it in excluded_source_handles\". I will review the routed sources for Ch3. Some might be better suited for Ch1 or Ch5 primarily. I will keep those that have specific metabolite mechanism content for Ch3.\nFor example, P0002 (Ecological stratification) is routed to Ch1 & Ch3. It mentions carbohydrate metabolism (SCFA). I can use it for SCFA functional potential.\nP0004 (Pancreatic) is routed to Ch1,2,3,5. It mentions 3-IAA/AhR. I can use it for Ch3 metabolite mechanism.\nI will try to retain most routed sources but focus the `substantive_threads` on the mechanism.\n\nLet's draft the `substantive_threads`.\n1. SCFAs: Context-dependent immunomodulation (HDAC inhibition vs GPCR).\n2. Inosine: Tumor-intrinsic UBA6 inhibition vs Immune cell A2AR activation.\n3. Bile Acids & Tryptophan: Nuclear receptor signaling (FXR, TGR5, AhR).\n4. Evidence Hierarchy: Plasma vs TME concentrations, Mouse vs Human mechanisms.\n\nI need to be careful with the `source_routing` data provided in the input. It's a long list. I will select the handles that are most relevant for the *mechanism* focus of Ch3.\nI will list the `source_handles` in the chapter proposal that are actually used for the arguments.\nI will also add `supplement_requests` if there are critical gaps (like TME inosine concentration) that need specific search, though the `tool_materials` already indicate this is 